# FIX (spec item 9.1 - "reputation link is broken"): the SPA-fallback
# problem this used to solve (a cold/fresh request for a client-side
# route like /reputation/<token>, /verify/:paymentId, or
# /onboard/:token falling through to a 404/login instead of reaching
# React Router) is now handled by wrangler.jsonc's own
# `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` setting instead.
#
# A `/*  /index.html  200` wildcard rule here used to do this job, but
# now that wrangler.jsonc handles it at the platform level, having
# BOTH active at once makes Cloudflare reject the whole deploy with
# "Invalid _redirects configuration: infinite loop detected" (the two
# fallback mechanisms fight over the same stripped path). Do not
# re-add a wildcard rule here - if the SPA fallback ever needs
# adjusting, do it in wrangler.jsonc, not here.
